        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Swaps the specified coordinate axis which are assumed to be labeled 0=x, 1=y, and 2=z.</para>
<sect1 id="group___c_s_m_pglobal_functions_1arguments">
<title>Input Arguments</title><para>The two integer arguments refer to the axis which shall be changed. <linebreak/>
</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="group___c_s_m_pglobal_enums_1application">
<title>Application Examples</title><para>To adapt surface data to another frame of reference.</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="group___c_s_m_pglobal_functions_1messages">
<title>Messages</title><para>If the axes do not exist (are below 0 or greater than 2) the method will quit emitting a message. </para>
</sect1>
